    {
      "id": "xw33vdc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Discovery of the Cell"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Robert Hooke discovered cells in 1665 by examining thin slices of cork under a microscope.",
        "Cell Theory was proposed by Matthias Schleiden and Theodor Schwann, and later expanded by Rudolf Virchow.",
        "Cells are broadly classified into Prokaryotes (lacking a defined nucleus) and Eukaryotes (having a true membrane-bound nucleus).",
        "The cell membrane is a selectively permeable barrier composed of a phospholipid bilayer and proteins.",
        "Plant cells differ from animal cells by having a rigid cellulose cell wall, chloroplasts, and a large central vacuole."
      ],
      "id": "8vf6l3x"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s6akb8z",
      "content": "• Robert Hooke discovered the cell in 1665 while observing cork under a microscope."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "os6ffhd",
      "content": "• He described the small compartments as 'cells'."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z04fnp4",
      "content": "• Anton van Leeuwenhoek later observed living cells using a microscope."
    },
    {
      "id": "k5xnobr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Cell Theory"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7stmjcr",
      "content": "• All living organisms are composed of cells."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kn33f8n",
      "content": "• The cell is the basic unit of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7xvp03l",
      "content": "• All cells arise from pre-existing cells."
    },
    {
